2026-05-22 14:06:09,232 | AGENT | TechnicalArchitect Agent answered: Our current technical stack can meet the integration requirements with existing systems using API interfaces, as we have experience with various API standards such as REST, GraphQL, and SOAP, and API gateways like Kong and Apigee. We also have experience with message brokers like Apache Kafka and RabbitMQ, which can help with integrating with business software, EDM, and user directories.

In terms of response time, our typical performance benchmarks show a p95 response time of 1800 ms, which is lower than the required 2 seconds. However, to guarantee high availability of 99.9%, we will need to ensure that our architecture is designed with redundancy and failover capabilities in mind.

