Nexus Engineering S.r.l., through its consortium, proposes an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in their daily missions for the City of Belval. Our solution integrates technical expertise, security compliance, legal adherence, budget optimization, AI innovation, and sustainability practices to meet the City's requirements. We leverage our experience with specific technologies like Mistral 7B, SecNumCloud, Docker, Kubernetes, Terraform, and Prometheus to ensure high availability, performance, and security.

# Understanding of Requirements
The City of Belval seeks an artificial intelligence solution that assists municipal agents in accessing information, drafting administrative contents, instructing files, and ensuring continuity of processing while adhering to regulatory requirements such as GDPR, ensuring explicability, transparency, and security. The solution must integrate with existing systems, ensure high availability (99.9%), and optimize costs within a 3 million euro budget over 4 years.

# Proposed Solution
Our proposed solution is built around a microservices-based architecture utilizing containerization with Docker and orchestration with Kubernetes (K8s) to ensure scalability and high availability. We will deploy on SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure, leveraging our experience with cloud providers like Outscale and OVHcloud within the EU. For integration with existing systems such as business software, EDM, and user directories, we will use API interfaces (REST, GraphQL, SOAP) and message brokers like Apache Kafka.

To meet the performance requirement of a response time lower than 2 seconds, our architecture is designed with redundancy and failover capabilities in mind. Our typical performance benchmarks show a p95 response time of 1800 ms, which meets this requirement. We will also implement network security design patterns like Zero-trust and VLAN segmentation to ensure the security of the solution.

For AI components, we propose deploying models like Mistral 7B, which is self-hostable, has strong performance in French-language tasks, and can be fine-tuned using techniques such as LoRA or QLoRA. To reduce energetic consumption, we will apply quantization methods like INT8, reducing energy consumption by about 80% without significant performance degradation.

Our solution ensures GDPR compliance through strict data residency within the EU, anonymisation tools like Microsoft Presidio, and implementation of data subject rights. We guarantee no automated decisions without explicit validation by an agent, aligning with regulatory demands.

From a legal standpoint, our standard legal basis for GDPR compliance is under Article 6(1)(e), and we support Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIA). Our operations are intra-EU, eliminating the need for Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs) or adequacy decisions.

While specific budget details were not provided in the context, our pricing model targets a gross margin percentage of 28, with an minimum acceptable margin percentage of 18. To optimize costs, we can adjust standard daily rates, infrastructure margin, or software licence resale margin as needed.

Our approach to sustainability includes partnerships with green hosting providers like OVHcloud and Scaleway, powered by 100% renewable energy. Digital sobriety practices such as INT8/INT4 model quantisation, auto-scaling, query result caching, and a green IT hardware procurement policy reduce energy consumption. On average, our solutions achieve a typical energy reduction of 35% versus baseline.

# Unaddressed Requirements
The specific annual cost of exploitation and detailed breakdown of the 3 million euro budget over 4 years were not addressed due to lack of information in the provided context.

# Conclusion
Nexus Engineering S.r.l. offers a comprehensive solution that integrates AI innovation, security compliance, legal adherence, budget optimization, and sustainability practices to meet the City of Belval's requirements for an artificial intelligence assistance tool. By leveraging our expertise and experience with specific technologies and methodologies, we are confident in our ability to deliver a high-quality solution that enhances municipal services while adhering to regulatory and environmental standards.
